  "notes": "{奪|うば}う is a godan verb meaning 'to snatch,' 'to rob,' or 'to take by force.' It implies forceful or aggressive taking, often against someone's will.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- {奪|うば}う is transitive (takes a direct object)\n- Passive: {奪|うば}われる (to have something taken/snatched)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- ⟦{命|いのち}→命：02371_inochi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{奪|うば}う: to take someone's life\n- ⟦{目|め}→目：00525_me⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{奪|うば}う: to captivate (literally 'steal one's eyes')\n- ⟦{心|こころ}→心：01321_kokoro⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{奪|うば}う: to steal someone's heart\n- ⟦{自由|じゆう}→自由：01148_jiyuu⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{奪|うば}う: to take away freedom\n- ⟦{時間|じかん}→時間：00468_jikan⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{奪|うば}う: to take up someone's time\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{盗|ぬす}む→盗む：01166_nusumu⟧: to steal (secretly, covertly)\n- ⟦{取|と}る→取る：00565_toru⟧: to take (neutral)\n- ⟦{強奪|ごうだつ}する→強奪：12501_goudatsu⟧: to rob (formal/literary)",
